# Project Collaboration Standards

- Do not create explanatory, diagnostic, tutorial, or placeholder UI when implementing a feature unless the user explicitly requests that UI.
- Keep code approachable for teammates who write and maintain it manually.
- Add concise comments around non-obvious algorithms, state transitions, engine behavior, coordinate conversions, and other logic that may be difficult to understand.
- Prefer comments that explain intent and reasoning. Do not narrate self-explanatory statements or overwhelm simple code with comments.
- Use English for all repository content, including code, identifiers, comments, UI text, documentation, resource names, commit-related text, and generated assets.
- Do not add Chinese text to project files.
